HST Office: a Writer document's number formats aggregate is created once, also when two threads ask for it.

SwXTextDocument::queryInterface, getTypes and getSomething create the aggregated number formats
supplier (m_xNumFormatAgg) on first use and are called without the SolarMutex. A UNO bridge thread
(a script or converter driving the office over a pipe or socket) and the main thread (an extension
inspecting the document, here the session heartbeat and the "Phiên bản trước" job on OnModifyChanged)
asked a newly loaded document at the same moment: both saw no aggregate, both created one, one
reference was assigned over the other while it was still in use, and the heap broke later at unrelated
places ("malloc(): unsorted double linked list corrupted", SIGSEGV releasing a freed document over
the bridge). Converting 1602 .docx files in one office with the bundled extension crashed in every
run; with the creation serialised by a lock no run crashed. The lock is recursive because setting the
delegator may query the document again, and Invalidate/InitNewDoc take it so the doc shell and the
aggregate are never read half reset.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sw_uibase_uno (testNumberFormatsSupplierConcurrentQuery).
